<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#aircraft-carrier">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aircraft carrier</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as fleet carriers</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">An aircraft carrier is a warship designed to carry, launch and recover aircraft, serving as a mobile air base at sea. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/empire-of-japan">Empire of Japan</a> built one of the world's most capable carrier fleets in the interwar years and used it in the attack on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/attack-on-pearl-harbor">Pearl Harbor</a> in 1941. The loss of four fleet carriers at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-midway">Battle of Midway</a> in 1942 was a turning point in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>'s war in the Pacific.</p></div>
